HST Office: the remaining keys of the familiar office suite that only need a binding (owner rule 2026-11-15: every
shortcut matches the reference suite 100 %; data/ribbon/shortcuts-office-parity.json).

- HST Writer: Shift+F12 saves (was Bullets), Ctrl+F12 opens (was Insert Table), Ctrl+Shift+F12 prints (was Numbering
  off). Bullets, Insert Table and Numbering stay on the ribbon, the menus and their other keys.
- HST Writer: Ctrl+Alt+Shift+V inserts the AutoText entry whose name is before the cursor, as F3 (owner decision
  2026-11-15, replacing the 2026-11-14 plain-text paste on that key). Paste Unformatted Text stays in Edit ▸ Paste
  Special and on the ribbon, without a key, as in the reference suite.
- HST Sheets: Ctrl+Shift+F opens Format Cells on the Font tab (was Repeat Search on Windows and Linux; the find bar and
  Find & Replace still search), Ctrl+Alt+L reapplies the filter and sort of the range (.uno:DataAreaRefresh repeats
  the range's query, sort and subtotals, as the suite's Reapply).
- HST Slides and HST Draw: Ctrl+F2 opens the Print page of the File panel with its live preview, as Ctrl+P (the suite's
  Ctrl+F2 opens that same page).
- macOS: the keys of the suite's Mac edition (its published shortcut lists) where they are not simply Cmd+...: Writer
  Control+H Find & Replace, Cmd+Option+F footnote (was Find & Replace), Cmd+Option+E endnote (was Extension Manager);
  Sheets Control+H Find & Replace, F7 spelling, Cmd+Shift+F AutoFilter, Cmd+Shift+K / Cmd+Shift+J group / ungroup;
  Slides Cmd+Shift+H Find & Replace, F7 spelling, Cmd+T font dialog (was Styles), Cmd+Control+V Paste Special; Draw
  Cmd+Shift+H Find & Replace, F7 spelling. Windows and Linux keep their keys.
All platforms otherwise: on macOS the keys are Cmd+... as usual. Checked by scripts/check-keytips-parity.py.
License: modified upstream files keep their license (MPL-2.0).
